ISSUES
    REBOOT_MOTHER = #1
    GUIDE_HISTORY = #2
    FIRST_TASK = #3
    BOOTSTRAP_EXECUTOR_HISTORY = #4
    FIRST_TASK_PARENT = #1

TOPOLOGY
    mother = goal and accepted scope
    child = independently finishable delivery
    grandchild = concrete subdivision only when needed
    Task declares PARENT and mother lists children
    native GitHub sub-issue link = use when available, report when absent
    current #3 -> #1 = explicit textual relationship, native link not established
    histories = independent records, not executable Tasks or children by implication

GUIDE
    keeps decisions and factual chronology in #2
    creates Task contract from templates/task.pot
    identifies scope and evidence; does not duplicate shell documentation in prompts
    chooses executors by availability/capability, without permanent preference
    records accepted/rejected/deferred findings with reason

EXECUTOR
    has own history issue, created when first participating
    records Task/HEAD/completed/validation/limitations/next
    successor references previous executor history and continues same Task
    local checkpoint carries operational detail; GitHub carries public summary
    no secrets, raw credentials or private provider state in either

DECISION
    TYPE = <ACCEPT | REJECT | DEFER | REQUEST_CHANGE>
    TASK = <issue>
    HEAD = <sha-or-NOT_APPLICABLE>
    EVIDENCE = <links>
    REASON = <concise-explanation>
    NEXT = <bounded-action>

LIMITS
    no new child merely to repeat status
    no mandatory cleaning of every historical issue before product progress
    no merge/release/destructive cleanup without specific authorization
